   P-1 CLOSED by CL-1   Find one radius for the Plasm cell that keeps both its full training run and a 5 percent behaviour bound.
   P-2 CLOSED by CL-2   Tune one radius of the Frobenius ball until it is both safe and useful, on the 24 hosts of the calibration record.
   P-3 CLOSED by CL-3   Admit grafts by a threshold on a published, fixed probe set, on the 11 MLP hosts certified.
   P-4 CLOSED by CL-4   Ship the two-check admission rule as the whole admission test.
   P-5 open             Splice a reversal skill without an attention graft.
   P-6 open             Admit a graft as a behaviour claim one input can refute, with probes drawn after commitment (the committed-behaviour-change record).
   P-7 CLOSED by CL-5   Keep one radius and trade the Frobenius ball for a distance between the singular-value distance and the Frobenius distance, such as the ball after the best relabelling of hidden units or a scaled optimal-transport distance between neuron sets, on the 12 MLP hosts.
   P-8 CLOSED by CL-6   Admit a copy of a cell rounded to 5, 6 or 7 bits, by even levels per matrix, with a Frobenius radius around the float cell, on the 12 MLP hosts.
   P-9 CLOSED by CL-7   Let a cell rounded to 5 to 7 bits, by even levels per matrix, change one weight by one grid step and certify that first step with the ball of Theorem 1, on the 12 MLP hosts.
   P-10 open             Let a rounded cell adapt off its grid, with a float side update, and judge the result by behaviour.

